{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.GradedHeckeEnergyTruncationBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.GradedHeckeEnergyTruncationBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.graded_hecke_energy_work_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.graded_hecke_energy_work_bound","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/graded-hecke-energy-truncation-bound.lean#L120-L134","doc":"**Computational corollary.**  Numerical evaluation of\n`tr_M(T_w(β_K), q_0) = P_K(q_0)` only requires enumerating the\ngrades `d ∈ {0, 1, …, ℓ(K, q_0)}`.  The naive partition-indexed\nenumeration over all `p(n)` partitions of the `n` strands of\n`β_K` is replaced by an enumeration over at most\n`ℓ(K, q_0) + 1` effective grades.\n\nSchematic statement: the work bound depends on the confinement\nlevel instance, not on `p(n)`.  Quantitative speedup table is\nin the `.md` companion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.graded_hecke_energy_finite_support","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.graded_hecke_energy_finite_support","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/graded-hecke-energy-truncation-bound.lean#L103-L118","doc":"**Finite-support corollary.** The set of grades carrying\nnonzero coefficients is contained in `{0, 1, …, ℓ(K, q_0)}`,\na finite set of size `ℓ(K, q_0) + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.graded_hecke_energy_truncation_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.graded_hecke_energy_truncation_bound","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/graded-hecke-energy-truncation-bound.lean#L81-L101","doc":"**Graded Hecke energy truncation bound.**\nConditional on the GS-filtration descent\n(`GradedMarkovTraceDescent` class) and a confinement-level\ninstance, the mass-spectrum generating function `P_K(q)` has\nnonzero coefficients **only** on grades `d ∈ {0, 1, …, ℓ(K, q_0)}`.\n\nThe theorem statement is the contrapositive support claim:\nevery grade `d` outside that finite range has coefficient zero.\n\nPer AGENTS.md §3b-cond, this is a *rigorous conditional result*:\nfully verified by Lean modulo the named class instances which\naxiomatise (i) the descent (`conj:gs-graded-markov-trace-existence`)\nand (ii) the confinement-level value (`def:confinement-level`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:graded-hecke-energy-truncation-bound","label":"prop:graded-hecke-energy-truncation-bound","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/graded-hecke-energy-truncation-bound.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.GradedMarkovTraceDescent.vanishes_below","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.GradedMarkovTraceDescent.vanishes_below","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/graded-hecke-energy-truncation-bound.lean#L76-L76","doc":"The descended trace also vanishes on negative grades (the\nKLR principal-projective system has no negative-grade\ngenerators in the highest-weight cone). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.GradedMarkovTraceDescent.vanishes_above","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.GradedMarkovTraceDescent.vanishes_above","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/graded-hecke-energy-truncation-bound.lean#L71-L71","doc":"The descent property: the descended trace vanishes on every\ngrade beyond the confinement level.  This is the Lean\ncounterpart of the homological boundedness of `𝔐_K` under\nthe jet/filtration order — `J^{ℓ+1}(q) = 0` for\n`ℓ = ConfinementLevel.level K`, so any mass-spectrum\ncoefficient `P.coeffs d` for `d` outside `{0, …, ℓ}`\nnecessarily vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.GradedMarkovTraceDescent.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.GradedMarkovTraceDescent.mk","kind":"ctor","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/graded-hecke-energy-truncation-bound.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.GradedMarkovTraceDescent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.GradedMarkovTraceDescent","kind":"class","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/graded-hecke-energy-truncation-bound.lean#L57-L77","doc":"The graded Markov trace from GS-filtration descent\n(`conj:gs-graded-markov-trace-existence`).  Stated as a class\nThe truncation theorem is conditional per AGENTS.md §3b-cond\non this conjecture's content.  An instance asserts that the\ndescent holds — i.e. the Markov trace descends to a sequence\n`tr_{M, ℓ}` along the GS filtration `J^•(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassSpectrum.coeffs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassSpectrum.coeffs","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/graded-hecke-energy-truncation-bound.lean#L55-L55","doc":"The grade-d coefficient `c_d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassSpectrum.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassSpectrum.mk","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/graded-hecke-energy-truncation-bound.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassSpectrum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassSpectrum","kind":"structure","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/graded-hecke-energy-truncation-bound.lean#L46-L55","doc":"The mass-spectrum generating function as an indexed sequence of\ncoefficients `c_d ∈ ℕ` (the microstate degeneracies; non-negative\nintegers by `rem:categorical-mass-positivity`).  Stored as a\nfunction on integer grades `d`, with the truncation bound\nenforced by `bound_holds`.  This is a schematic encoding —\nthe genuine `Σ c_d q^d` Laurent polynomial lives in\n`rem:mass-spectrum-generating-function`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ConfinementLevel.level","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ConfinementLevel.level","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/graded-hecke-energy-truncation-bound.lean#L44-L44","doc":"The confinement level — a natural number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ConfinementLevel.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ConfinementLevel.mk","kind":"ctor","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/graded-hecke-energy-truncation-bound.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ConfinementLevel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ConfinementLevel","kind":"class","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/graded-hecke-energy-truncation-bound.lean#L36-L44","doc":"The confinement level `ℓ(K, q_0) ∈ ℕ` of a knot/braid `K` at\nthe substrate value `q_0`.  Defined here as a structural input\nvia class hypothesis; the genuine definition lives in\n`def:confinement-level` (homological boundedness of `𝔐_K`\nunder the jet/filtration order).  Concrete model: any natural\nnumber, default 0 (the trivial knot). ","signatureChunk":0}]}